>
  <p class="lead-para">
    <strong>The skills needed for your first job in India are not just the technical skills on your resume — they are the foundational, everyday skills nobody formally taught you: clear communication, basic email etiquette, comfortable spreadsheet use, and realistic time management.</strong>
    These are the skills a manager judges you on in your first weeks, regardless of whether you are an
    engineer, a marketer, an accountant, or a customer support executive. Most freshers spend their prep time
    on the technical side alone and are caught off guard by how much the rest of it counts.
  </p>

