  <h2 id="next-step">Where to build these skills next</h2>

  <p>
    These foundational skills work alongside your career-track skills, not instead of them. Once you have both
    in place, the next question is how to actually get noticed with them. For the positioning and proof-of-work
    side of standing out once these basics are solid, see
    <a href="/blog/job-search/how-to-stand-out-as-a-fresher-india/">how to stand out as a fresher in India</a>.
    If you are preparing for an interview right now, see
    <a href="/blog/interviews/interview-preparation-for-freshers-india/">interview preparation for freshers in India</a>
    for how to build answers around your academic projects and internships. And if your resume is not yet
    reflecting any of this, see
    <a href="/blog/resume/resume-tips-for-freshers-india/">resume tips for freshers in India</a>.
  </p>

  <p>
    If you are unsure which of these gaps is actually holding you back, or how they connect to the specific
    role you are targeting, a session with
    <a href="https://futurecareerschool.com/services/career-counselling-and-career-guidance/">career guidance</a>
    can help you build a focused plan around unlocking higher-income opportunities sooner, instead of guessing
    at what to fix first. Not sure which roles genuinely fit how you like to work? Start with the free
    <a href="https://futurecareerschool.com/services/assessments">career and skill assessments</a> to see where
    your skill portfolio already has an edge, and where it still needs work.
  </p>

